# Page functions: scripts for a page of encoders, when the firmware has one.  `page "LABEL"` lists a function on that page
# (label 1..8 characters); its `param`s (at most 6) are the encoders A..F.  A page function takes no argument and
# may not use the card, the Static slots (dir ext match file.* static.* slots.*).  The page runs it on the
# current track again each time an encoder moves, on a pattern that has been put back as the hands left it.

# A Euclidean pattern page as a script: two euclidean rhythms (pl1 pulses rotated by r1, pl2 pulses rotated by r2)
# spread over the pattern, combined by op (0 OR, 1 XOR, 2 AND, 3 SUB = the first without the second), the result
# rotated by tro; it only adds red trigs, on steps that have none (tr.add).
# Differences with the page: the length is pat.len (a page could spread over the track's length), and a script
# cannot hold the trigs it added as a separate layer: that is the page's job (snapshot, print, discard).
def eucl
  page "EUCL"
  param pl1 4 0 64
  param pl2 0 0 64
  param op 0 0 3
  param r1 0 -63 63
  param r2 0 -63 63
  param tro 0 -63 63
  a pat.len                          # n, the length of the rhythm
  each:
    if not has.trig i:
      b wrap sub i tro 1 a           # the step this one comes from before the final rotation tro
      c er.r pl1 a r1 b              # er.r k n r s: rhythm of k pulses over n steps, rotated by r
      d er.r pl2 a r2 b
      if eq op 0:
        if or c d: tr.add i
      elif eq op 1:
        if xor c d: tr.add i
      elif eq op 2:
        if and c d: tr.add i
      else:
        if and c not d: tr.add i

# The simplest page: a density, in percent of the free steps (named pdens: dens is a name of BOOMBAP.OTY).
def pdens
  page "DENS"
  param pct 25 0 100
  each:
    if not has.trig i:
      prob pct: tr.add i
